<aetgt:getResponse xmlns:aetgt="http://schemas.active-endpoints.com/appmodules/repository/2010/10/avrepository.xsd"
                   xmlns:types1="http://schemas.active-endpoints.com/appmodules/repository/2010/10/avrepository.xsd">
   <types1:Item>
      <types1:EntryId>xpZXrmJaYOBu7TJpkrH1WV-gt-00000010-2026-07-27T17:44:00.000Z::pd.xml</types1:EntryId>
      <types1:Name>ErrorAlert_Process</types1:Name>
      <types1:MimeType>application/xml+process</types1:MimeType>
      <types1:Description>Build guide 4.13-4.14. Shared fault handler target: formats a failure notification for a failed employee run.</types1:Description>
      <types1:AppliesTo/>
      <types1:Tags/>
      <types1:VersionLabel>1.0</types1:VersionLabel>
      <types1:State>CURRENT</types1:State>
      <types1:ProcessGroup/>
      <types1:CreatedBy>abdul.mannuru@hubbard.com.dev</types1:CreatedBy>
      <types1:CreationDate>2026-07-27T17:44:00Z</types1:CreationDate>
      <types1:ModifiedBy/>
      <types1:PublicationStatus>unpublished</types1:PublicationStatus>
      <types1:Entry>
         <process xmlns="http://schemas.active-endpoints.com/appmodules/screenflow/2010/10/avosScreenflow.xsd"
                  xmlns:tfm="http://schemas.active-endpoints.com/appmodules/screenflow/2021/04/taskflowModel.xsd"
                  xmlns:list="urn:activevos:spi:list:functions"
                  GUID="xpZXrmJaYOBu7TJpkrH1WV"
                  displayName="ErrorAlert_Process"
                  name="ErrorAlert_Process"
                  overrideAPIName="false">
            <parameterSet xmlns="http://schemas.active-endpoints.com/appmodules/screenflow/2021/04/taskflowModel.xsd"/>
            <appliesTo/>
            <description>Build guide 4.13/4.14: receives structured fault details from ProcessOneEmployee_Process's fault handler and formats a notification. NOT WIRED TO AN EMAIL CONNECTOR YET - see notes.</description>
            <tags/>
            <generator>Informatica Process Designer 11</generator>
            <input>
               <parameter description="Employee identifier the failure occurred for, empty if the failure happened before an employee was resolved" name="in_XRefCode" required="false" type="string">
                  <options>
                     <option name="required">false</option>
                  </options>
               </parameter>
               <parameter description="Name of the sub-process/step that raised the fault" name="in_FailedStepName" required="false" type="string">
                  <options>
                     <option name="required">false</option>
                  </options>
               </parameter>
               <parameter description="Fault code/message from the failing call" name="in_ErrorMessage" required="false" type="string">
                  <options>
                     <option name="required">false</option>
                  </options>
               </parameter>
            </input>
            <output>
               <field description="Formatted alert subject line" name="out_Subject" type="string">
                  <options>
                     <option name="required">false</option>
                  </options>
               </field>
               <field description="Formatted alert body" name="out_Body" type="string">
                  <options>
                     <option name="required">false</option>
                  </options>
               </field>
            </output>
            <notes>Hand-authored against the CPD-Dayforce Functional Design &amp; API Build Guide v1.0 and verified against real IICS Process Designer 11 exports - see README_IICS_BUILD_NOTES.md.
OPEN ITEM: this process only formats the alert (Assignment step below) - it does not yet call an Email/notification connector, because no such connector currently exists in this project's scope to reference by a real serviceGUID (inventing one would fail import, per the lesson learned building the rest of this package). Once the client confirms recipients and format (build guide 4.14) and an Email connection/connector is created in this IICS org, add a &lt;service&gt; step here calling it (mirroring the SvcConn_get_post_dayforce/SvcConn_Get_Post_Cpd &lt;service&gt; pattern used throughout this package), mapping out_Subject/out_Body into its input fields.</notes>
            <deployment skipIfRunning="false" suspendOnFault="false" tracingLevel="none">
               <rest/>
            </deployment>
            <flow id="a">
               <start id="b">
                  <link id="l1" targetId="asn-format"/>
               </start>
               <assignment id="asn-format">
                  <title>Format alert</title>
                  <operation source="formula" to="output.out_Subject">
                     <expression language="XQuery">'Dayforce-CPD integration failure: XRefCode ' || $input.in_XRefCode || ' at ' || $input.in_FailedStepName</expression>
                  </operation>
                  <operation source="formula" to="output.out_Body">
                     <expression language="XQuery">'Employee XRefCode: ' || $input.in_XRefCode || '&#10;Failed step: ' || $input.in_FailedStepName || '&#10;Error message: ' || $input.in_ErrorMessage</expression>
                  </operation>
                  <link id="l2" targetId="c"/>
               </assignment>
               <end id="c">
                  <title>End</title>
               </end>
            </flow>
         </process>
      </types1:Entry>
      <types1:GUID>xpZXrmJaYOBu7TJpkrH1WV</types1:GUID>
      <types1:DisplayName>ErrorAlert_Process</types1:DisplayName>
   </types1:Item>
   <types1:CurrentServerDateTime>2026-07-27T17:46:15.000Z</types1:CurrentServerDateTime>
</aetgt:getResponse>
